From 2b2c821fbcc28412409d0a257650f1daca86e9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shapey Review <review@shapey.local>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:13:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] fix(online): correct for device clock skew using
 serverNow

Every online deadline (turnEndsAt, reviewEndsAt, reveals[].endsAt,
pendingEffect, poll endsAt, tile movingUntil) is a server wall-clock
timestamp, but both clients compared them against the device's own
Date.now(). A phone with a wrong clock (minutes off is common) would
see online turns expire early, freeze, or show wrong poll countdowns
by exactly the skew.

- worker: gameViewForPlayer/gameViewForSpectator/audiencePollSnapshot
  now include serverNow (default Date.now()), passed once per
  broadcast so all sockets in a room share one timestamp
- game client: applyOnlineState() measures serverClockOffset from each
  snapshot; every online deadline read (turn clock, study reveal,
  spawn reveals, poll countdown, movingUntil, reconnect restores) goes
  through serverToLocal()
- audience page: same offset measurement in renderGameState(); HUD
  clock, memorize cue and pollSecondsLeft convert through it
- worker test pins the serverNow field on both view builders
